+test(
+  "a slow reconcile failure must not collapse the exponential backoff into a ~1s hammer",
+  async () => {
+    // openedAt used to be stamped at the TOP of onOpen, i.e. BEFORE the reconcile.
+    // A reconcile that failed SLOWLY (a gateway timeout) therefore counted as
+    // ">= OPENCODE_SSE_MIN_OPEN_MS open", reset `attempt` to 0 on every iteration,
+    // and turned the exponential backoff into a fixed ~1s reconnect hammer against
+    // an already-sick door. Very likely why the production incident was as bad as it
+    // was. Stamping openedAt AFTER the reconcile leaves it undefined on a throw, so
+    // a failed attempt always keeps the exponential climbing.
